Subject: CPMS I03E Corpus Replay Report Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 0cab5532-8e59-4598-af52-546ff508f0d4
@ [canonical_specification_uuid] b13ea7b3-0ff6-4fcc-aed3-3eaec4a786c5

& [Problem] I03D intentionally emits independent observations and cannot itself state agreement coverage or replay
& [Rejected1] compare reader booleans because equal outcomes can concern different rules or violate both expectations
& [Rejected2] require literal rule-id equality because schema and typed readers use different vocabularies
& [Rejected3] treat all rejected-rejected pairs as agreement because unrelated failures would become false confirmation
& [Rejected4] infer semantic validity or compatibility from syntactic agreement because residual and authority gates are independent
& [Rejected5] claim exhaustive equivalence from a finite corpus because uncovered language behavior remains possible
& [Rejected6] hash a report containing its own digest because the identity would be circular
& [Rejected7] clone the first report as replay because it would test copying rather than deterministic recomputation
& [Selected] common claims with dual witness mappings obligation-driven finite coverage two fresh canonical cores and a separate replay envelope
& [Reason] the selected form makes every inference edge inspectable while keeping scope authority and determinism honest
& [Disposition] is formation_justified_implementation_not_justified
